# Programming Tip: Using a loop within your main if condition statement in C++
In many instances when you have to repeat yourself multiple times when writing a set of if condition statements in your code, there is a technique you can employ to reduce the same amount of copy and paste code. It involves writing a small subroutine or loop within your if condition which will call itself multiple times inside the same if conditional statement. Here is an example in C++ (GCC compiler):

\begin{code}
if(condition){
    if(loop){
        loop();   //execute subroutine here inside same conditional statement
    }
} else {   //condition did not trigger loop() subroutine
}
\end{code}

Where loop can be defined as:

\begin{code}
void loop(){}  //execute same if conditions here inside loop block.
\end{code}

